    "kit_id": "poe1-animate-weapon",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "Element: base skill is physical but the meta variant (Ranged Arms) is a POISON minion build; poison here is a necromancer/corruption register -> shadow family + poison ailment lane (crosswalk §1 poison-row: shadow when corruption-themed, minions=necro). Geometry: the animated weapons are transient proxies (totem geometry = placed autonomous entity); Bladefall is the multi_projectile feeder. PROXY_FISSION routes 'one summoning action -> many transient proxies'. THE MISSED IDENTITY: 'loot lying on the ground literally becomes ammunition; the drop stream is the resource pool' — engine proxies summon from mana/corpses, NOT from ground-dropped item entities. That resource-substrate (ground-item-consumption-as-summon-fuel) has no engine lane; docketed. A Poison-Ranged-AW player would notice their summons are no longer gated by/fed from the loot-drop stream — the flavor that made this kit iconic.",
